From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -read_latency, registered read
 addresses
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

-read_latency 1 registers every read port's address: a plain
positive-edge flop per address bit, found by its ff group, in the
address inverter's cell; the data follows a cycle after the address,
as XiangShan's register files read. Where the flop gives the address
inverted (asap7's DFFHQNx1) the decoders take the flop's output as the
complement and the inverter makes the true literal, so no cell is
added. The behavioral model registers the addresses the same way. Not
with -column_mux_ratio above 1 or with read/write ports (RAM-0072).

Tested: src/ram/test/read_latency_asap7.tcl.

Commit 7 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
